{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2240","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2240","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2240\",\"parent_revision\":\"0a48552bad719c07693365db02ed97b56ac500a9\",\"root_revision\":\"09a5362eaf27fe4e68419e320aedf29838c6ee49e05a9fb21c14caddd1b92f4f\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**Status: APPROVED-WITH-GAPS**\\n\\nFunctional intent is clearly stated: a `--landing single-pr | per-wave-pr` mode parameter that, when set to `per-wave-pr`, creates a branch per wave, opens a PR against the integration branch, polls CI to green, then squash-merges before the next wave starts.\\n\\n**AVAILABLE (sourced from primary files):**\\n\\n- Current workflow model: `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-milestone/SKILL.md` lines 22\u201396. Single integration branch, per-wave local merges, one final PR at Step 9. Verified.\\n- `DispatchPlan` model at `plugins/development-harness/dispatch_schema/core/models.py` \u2014 fields: `milestone`, `conflict_groups`, `waves`, `quality_gates`. No `landing_mode` field exists. Verified.\\n- `dispatch_state.py` (`DispatchStateManager`) SQLite schema at lines 56\u201399: `waves` table has `(milestone, wave_num, status, started_at, completed_at)`. `items` table has no `pr_number` or `ci_status` column. Verified.\\n- `gh pr create` / `gh pr checks` / `gh pr merge` \u2014 established infrastructure per CLAUDE.md and `/gh` skill.\\n- Prior art pattern: `research/skill-generation-tools/composio-codebase-migrate.md` \u2014 batched PRs (~25 files each), CI polling, merge-then-loop.\\n- SAM autonomy field precedent: `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/models.py` line 329 shows `autonomy: Literal[\\\"full_auto\\\", \\\"checkpoint\\\", \\\"per_task\\\"]` as an additive field with default preserving backward compatibility. Same pattern applies here.\\n\\n**DERIVABLE (follows from available sources):**\\n\\n- `landing_mode` field can be modeled as `Literal[\\\"single-pr\\\", \\\"per-wave-pr\\\"]` with default `\\\"single-pr\\\"` to preserve backward compatibility, following the `autonomy` field precedent.\\n- Wave-PR branch naming: `milestone/{N}-wave-{W}` derived from existing `milestone/{N}-{slug}` convention.\\n- Failing CI on wave PR should halt subsequent waves \u2014 the existing `InvestigateFail` branch at Step 6a provides the escalation hook.\\n\\n**MISSING (required before execution):**\\n\\n- `dispatch_wave_status` MCP tool response shape: does it currently return a wave PR number? Grep of `server.py` for `dispatch_wave_status` found the function exists but the wave `pr_number` / `ci_status` columns are absent from the schema. Schema migration strategy for the SQLite `waves` table must be decided before implementation.\\n- CI polling timeout/retry policy: max wait time, back-off interval, and failure disposition for a wave PR that stays pending for an extended period.\\n- Whether `per-wave-pr` merges squash or merge-commit (item says squash; confirm this is the right default).\\n- Whether the new step (`6e-WaitCI`) blocks wave dispatch globally or only blocks the next wave from starting (distinction matters for error recovery).\\n- Whether `dispatch_create_plan` MCP tool call sites need updating to accept the new field, and whether existing dispatch plan YAML files with no `landing_mode` key must be forward-migrated or can be read as defaulting to `single-pr`.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **add per-wave pr-and-merge mode to work-milestone for reviewable batched landings** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Research entry: ./research/skill-generation-tools/composio-codebase-migrate.md \u2014 pattern: Batched Execution with Tracking (one PR per ~25 files, merge-then-loop)\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-05-10\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-05-14)\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n8/10 \u2014 Directly addresses a user-visible operational pain point (50-item milestone producing one unreviable diff). The Composio codebase-migrate pattern validates real-world demand. Unblocks teams who require PR-per-batch review cadence. Risk is bounded: `single-pr` default means zero behavior change for existing users. Existing CI gate infrastructure (`gh pr checks`) is already present in the project. Does not block other P1 items but is complementary to #975 (TeamCreate dispatch) and #2107 (post-PR CI auto-fix watcher).\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n- Blocks: Teams requiring human PR review before each wave proceeds cannot use `/work-milestone` for their workflow today. This is the only blocker path.\\n- Bottleneck: Large milestones (10+ items, 3+ waves) produce monolithic diffs that are not reviewable in practice. Regression bisection cost grows linearly with wave count when all waves are merged before the first CI signal.\\n- Cascade risk: `dispatch_schema/core/models.py` (`DispatchPlan`), `dispatch_state.py` schema, `backlog_core/server.py` (MCP tool), and `skills/work-milestone/SKILL.md` all need coordinated changes. Touching the SQLite schema requires a migration strategy.\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\n- Each wave's diff is independently reviewable \u2014 reviewer workload is bounded to one wave's scope.\\n- Regressions surface at the wave boundary (CI gate) rather than at final Land, when later waves have already built on top of the breaking change.\\n- Bisection and rollback are cheap: revert the single wave PR rather than unpicking N waves merged into an integration branch.\\n- Unlocks teams with review-gated merge policies (required reviewers, branch protection) who currently cannot use `/work-milestone`.\\n- Composio codebase-migrate pattern validation: proven approach for large-scale batched migrations at scale.\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nWhen `landing_mode: single-pr` (default): behavior is identical to today \u2014 no per-wave PRs are created, the integration branch is merged to main in one final step.\\n\\nWhen `landing_mode: per-wave-pr`: after each wave's worktree branches are merged locally into the integration branch (Step 6b), the accumulated delta is pushed as a branch `milestone/{N}-wave-{W}` and a PR is opened against the integration branch. The milestone orchestrator waits for CI checks to pass green on that PR, then squash-merges it. Only after merge does the next wave begin. If CI fails, subsequent waves do not start and a backlog item is created for the fix.\\n\\nThe measurable signal defined in the item (importable `DispatchPlan` field, `gh pr list` returning at least 2 wave PRs, dispatch DB rows with `pr_number` and `ci_status: green`) describes the observable state of a successful run.\\n\\n### Desired Structure\\n\\n- `DispatchPlan` in `dispatch_schema/core/models.py` has a `landing_mode` field with values `\\\"single-pr\\\" | \\\"per-wave-pr\\\"` and default `\\\"single-pr\\\"`.\\n- `DispatchStateManager` SQLite schema has `pr_number` and `ci_status` columns on the `waves` table (or a new `wave_prs` table).\\n- `dispatch_wave_status` MCP tool response includes `pr_number` and `ci_status` when `landing_mode: per-wave-pr`.\\n- `work-milestone/SKILL.md` workflow graph includes a Step 6e between WaveComplete and DiscoveryRelay that is active only in `per-wave-pr` mode.\\n- The step between wave completion and next-wave start is observable: a PR exists on GitHub, CI checks are visible, and the wave's dispatch state row reflects the outcome before the next wave starts.\\n- `groom-milestone` SKILL reads and passes `landing_mode` when creating a dispatch plan.\\n- Running the measurable signal command `gh pr list -R Jamie-BitFlight/claude_skills --state merged --search \\\"wave-\\\"` returns at least 2 PRs after a 2-wave run in `per-wave-pr` mode.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. `uv run python -c \\\"from dispatch_schema.core.models import DispatchPlan; print(DispatchPlan.model_fields['landing_mode'])\\\"` prints a field descriptor with default `single-pr` and no error.\\n2. A dispatch plan YAML with no `landing_mode` key is read by `dispatch_read` without error and returns `landing_mode: single-pr`.\\n3. A dispatch plan YAML with `landing_mode: per-wave-pr` is written and read back correctly via `dispatch_create_plan` and `dispatch_read`.\\n4. Running a 2-wave milestone in `per-wave-pr` mode: `gh pr list -R Jamie-BitFlight/claude_skills --state merged --search \\\"wave-\\\"` returns at least 2 PRs.\\n5. After each wave merges in `per-wave-pr` mode, `dispatch_wave_status` for that wave returns `pr_number` (non-null) and `ci_status: green`.\\n6. In `per-wave-pr` mode, if CI fails on a wave PR, the next wave does NOT start and a backlog item is created for the fix.\\n7. In `single-pr` mode (default), behavior is unchanged from the current workflow \u2014 no per-wave PRs are created, existing milestones run without modification.\\n8. `uv run pytest plugins/development-harness/tests/test_dispatch_schema/` passes with new tests for `landing_mode` field presence and round-trip serialization.\\n9. `uv run pytest plugins/development-harness/tests/test_dispatch_tools.py` passes including new tests for `dispatch_create_plan` accepting `landing_mode`.\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| Skill | /dh:work-milestone |\\n| Skill | /dh:groom-milestone |\\n| Skill | /gh |\\n| Prior work | plugins/development-harness/dispatch_schema/core/models.py |\\n| Prior work | plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/dispatch_state.py |\\n| Prior work | plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py (dispatch_wave_status, dispatch_create_plan) |\\n| Prior work | plugins/development-harness/skills/work-milestone/SKILL.md |\\n| Prior work | plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/models.py (autonomy field \u2014 design precedent) |\\n| Prior work | plugins/development-harness/tests/test_dispatch_schema/ |\\n| Prior work | plugins/development-harness/tests/test_dispatch_tools.py |\\n| Research | research/skill-generation-tools/composio-codebase-migrate.md |\\n| Agent | @dh:feature-researcher |\\n| Agent | @dh:codebase-analyzer |\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: None (self-contained; `gh` CLI infrastructure already present)\\n- Blocks: #2107 (post-PR CI auto-fix watcher) \u2014 that item's value increases when per-wave PRs exist as discrete merge targets\\n- Related: #975 (TeamCreate dispatch) \u2014 orthogonal but coordinatable; #1859 (autonomy modes) \u2014 sibling feature using same design pattern\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nMedium \u2014 Four coordinated change surfaces: (1) `dispatch_schema/core/models.py` adds one field (trivial), (2) `dispatch_state.py` SQLite schema gets two new columns with a migration path (small), (3) `backlog_core/server.py` MCP tool (`dispatch_wave_status`) adds `pr_number`/`ci_status` to response (small), (4) `work-milestone/SKILL.md` workflow graph adds Step 6e and the `per-wave-pr` branch (medium \u2014 mermaid graph update + CI poll logic). Test coverage for all four surfaces is required. The changes are additive and default-preserving, so integration risk is low.\\n\\n### Blockers\\n\\n- SQLite schema migration strategy for the `waves` table (add `pr_number TEXT`, `ci_status TEXT` columns, or introduce a `wave_prs` join table) must be decided before implementation begins. `DispatchStateManager.ensure_schema()` is idempotent \u2014 `ALTER TABLE IF NOT EXISTS` via executescript would be the appropriate extension point.\\n- CI polling timeout / retry policy is unspecified: how long to wait for a wave-PR's CI run to complete before declaring a failure? Back-off interval? These parameters must be confirmed before the Step 6e logic can be finalized.\\n- Whether the wave-PR merge strategy is squash (as stated in the item) or merge-commit must be confirmed \u2014 it affects the integration branch commit graph and bisect usability.\\n- Whether `dispatch_create_plan` MCP server (in `backlog_core/server.py`) needs a version-compatible `plan` input schema update, or whether Pydantic's `model_validate` handles the new optional field transparently (the latter is expected given the default, but must be verified with a test).\\n\\n### Questions for Human\\n\\n- What is the CI polling timeout per wave PR? (e.g., 30 minutes max, 30-second poll interval)\\n- On CI timeout (not failure \u2014 just still pending): halt milestone, retry, or skip wave and continue?\\n- Wave-PR merge strategy: squash (as stated in item) or merge-commit? Squash gives a cleaner integration branch but loses individual commit context.\\n- Should `per-wave-pr` PRs have required reviewers, or is CI-green the only merge gate? (Affects whether `gh pr merge --squash` can be called unattended.)\\n- Should `groom-milestone` prompt for `landing_mode`, or should it always be passed as a CLI argument to `/work-milestone`?\\n- When a wave CI fails and a backlog item is created for the fix, should the fix item be inserted into the current milestone (as the next wave) or created as a standalone future item?\\n\\n## Current State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`plugins/development-harness/skills/work-milestone/SKILL.md` lines 22\u201396 implements a single-integration-branch model. All wave worktree branches are merged into ONE integration branch (`milestone/{N}-{slug}`) and only that integration branch is pushed/PR'd at Step 9 (line 91 `git push origin main`). Per-wave merges (line 60 MergeLoop, line 62-71) happen locally \u2014 there is no per-wave PR creation, no per-wave CI run, no per-wave human review.\\n\\nThe dispatch plan model at `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/dispatch_state.py` tracks waves and items but has no concept of \\\"wave-PR\\\" or \\\"per-wave CI gate\\\". The `dispatch_wave_status` MCP tool reports completion but does not block on a green CI signal for each wave's merged delta.\\n\\nSymptom: a 50-item milestone produces one large diff at landing time. If wave 3 introduces a regression, it surfaces only at the final `Land` quality gate (line 85), after waves 4+ have already merged on top \u2014 making bisection and rollback expensive. There is no reviewer cadence option for teams who want PR-per-wave review like the Composio codebase-migrate pattern (~25 files per PR).\\n</div>\\n\\n## Target State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`work-milestone` SKILL accepts an autonomy/landing mode parameter (e.g., `--landing single-pr | per-wave-pr`) read from the dispatch plan or CLI. When mode is `per-wave-pr`:\\n\\n- Each completed wave creates a branch `milestone/{N}-wave-{W}` from the integration branch\\n- After Step 6c WaveComplete and 6d DiscoveryRelay: the wave branch is pushed and a PR opened against the integration branch using existing `gh pr create -R Jamie-BitFlight/claude_skills` infrastructure\\n- A new step `6e-WaitCI` polls `gh pr checks {PR}` until green, then merges the PR via `gh pr merge --squash`\\n- Failed CI on wave PR halts the milestone and creates a backlog item for fix; subsequent waves do not start\\n\\nField `landing_mode: \\\"single-pr\\\" | \\\"per-wave-pr\\\"` added to `DispatchPlan` model at `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/dispatch_state.py`.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Measurable Signal\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRun: `uv run python -c \\\"from backlog_core.dispatch_state import DispatchPlan; print(DispatchPlan.model_fields['landing_mode'])\\\"` \u2014 output shows the new field with default `single-pr`.\\n\\nRun a 2-wave milestone in `per-wave-pr` mode: `gh pr list -R Jamie-BitFlight/claude_skills --state merged --search \\\"wave-\\\"` returns at least 2 wave PRs. The dispatch state DB row for each wave includes `pr_number` and `ci_status: green` before the next wave starts.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"fddd4876b73e343f9c4fec7408b4e53d8004e0b4a22e99737710570d21bab88b\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPg3KeA\"}"}